# Spec 022 AC-5/AC-6/AC-7, automatic (spec 013): the yard, the self-check (prefab hierarchies against hand-written
# ones: its checksum lines must be the PC's bit for bit), then the showcase again: a crate picked by a touch, carried in
# the ship's hand and dropped where it was (keep world: the same position twice), the gun picked (depth 1), the debug
# draw, the ship destroyed with its children, a restart, the ship's children detached first; then the bench (AC-7's
# targets) and its verdict.
# PC:      nnh run hierarchy --pc --script examples/hierarchy/tests/check.nnhs
# Console: nnh run hierarchy --script examples/hierarchy/tests/check.nnhs   (Homebrew Launcher open, press Y)
#
# The expected lines below are the PC's (pc-debug). The showcase's lines change only if the yard or the moves below
# change; the checksum lines only if self_check.cpp or the hierarchy/prefabs/entities/transform modules change: then run
# `HIERARCHY_DEMO=check NNH_EXIT_AFTER_FRAMES=60 build/pc-debug/examples/hierarchy/hierarchy.exe`, copy its lines here
# and the values into kHierarchyCheckGolden/kHierarchyCheckpoints (self_check.hpp).
fail-on "] E "
fail-on "hierarchy: FAIL"
# A bench target missed fails the run too, but only at the bench's verdict line, logged after every bench number.
fail-on "hierarchy bench: FAIL"

# (The yard's first line is logged in frame 0, before the script starts: the restarts below expect it.)
wait 30
screenshot showcase

# The self-check (SELECT): 50 000 operations, a checksum every 10 000, then the verdict.
tap SELECT
expect "hierarchy: self-check started" 20
expect "hierarchy: 10000 sum D22B93EC" 60
expect "hierarchy: 20000 sum 9DB7C5E5" 60
expect "hierarchy: 30000 sum 820ED1D5" 60
expect "hierarchy: 40000 sum 5ED71B4D" 60
expect "hierarchy: 50000 sum 23DB5C36" 60
expect "hierarchy: PASS 23DB5C36" 30
wait 10
screenshot self-check

# Back to the showcase (SELECT): the yard again. The bottom screen shows it at zoom 0.5.
tap SELECT
expect "yard: restarted nodes 12" 20
wait 10
# The first crate (world 200,218 = bottom 100,109): picked, carried in the ship's hand, dropped where it was.
touch 100 109
expect "picked: crate slot 10 gen 2 depth 0 at 200,218" 5
wait 10
untouch
wait 10
tap X
expect "attached: crate to hand at 200,218" 10
wait 30
screenshot carried
tap X
expect "dropped: crate at 200,218" 10
wait 10
# The gun (its box around world 108,120 = bottom 54,60; its node at 104,120), over the ship: the child wins.
touch 54 60
expect "picked: gun slot 1 gen 2 depth 1 at 104,120" 5
wait 10
untouch
wait 10
tap DOWN
wait 10
screenshot debug-draw
tap DOWN
wait 10
# B: the ship goes, and its gun, muzzle and hand with it.
tap B
expect "destroyed: ship + 3 children" 10
wait 10
screenshot cascade
# X with the picked gun gone: a restart. Then D-Pad up detaches the ship's children first.
tap X
expect "yard: restarted nodes 12" 10
wait 10
tap UP
expect "detached: 2 children" 10
wait 10

# The bench (Y): five workloads of 300 frames, a line each, then the verdict (about 25 s).
tap Y
expect "hierarchy bench: started" 20
expect "hierarchy bench: pass_turn" 420
expect "hierarchy bench: pass_move" 420
expect "hierarchy bench: world_now" 420
expect "hierarchy bench: spawn" 420
expect "hierarchy bench: reparent" 420
expect "hierarchy bench: PASS" 30
wait 10
screenshot bench
